AB  - Immunohistochemistry (IHC) plays a pivotal role in cancer diagnostics, but manual scoring remains subjective and time-consuming. Recent advances in deep learning, particularly Vision Transformers (ViTs), offer transformative potential for automated and standardized IHC assessment. This paper presents an end-to-end framework leveraging multiscale Vision Transformers with Sharpness-Aware Minimization (SAM) to achieve spatially resolved quantification of tumor microenvironments (TMEs). This approach addresses critical needs for reproducibility and efficiency in pathological assessment, offering a scalable solution for modern cancer diagnostics. © 2025 IEEE.
