AD  - Oslo Metropolitan University (OsloMet), Department of Computer Science, Oslo, Norway
AB  - Accurate segmentation of retinal layers and pathological fluid regions in Spectral-Domain Optical Coherence Tomography (SD-OCT) images is critical for early diagnosis and monitoring of retinal diseases. However, this task is challenged by severe class imbalance, low contrast boundaries, and complex anatomical variations. In this paper, we propose a modified UU-Mamba architecture tailored for fine-grained retinal layer and fluid segmentation on the Duke SD-OCT dataset. Our approach integrates gated Mamba blocks for efficient global context modeling and introduces a customized Uncertainty-Aware Loss (UAL) function that strategically combines Tversky loss, class-specific Focal loss, and Cross-Entropy loss to mitigate class imbalance and enhance minority class sensitivity. We further employ Sharpness-Aware Minimization (SAM) during training to improve generalization across underrepresented structures. Experimental results demonstrate that our method achieves competitive performance, surpassing human expert segmentation, with an average Dice Similarity Coefficient (DSC) score of 0.85 compared to the human expert's 0.81. Extensive ablation studies validate the individual contributions of each proposed component, confirming the efficacy of our tailored loss design and regularization strategy in enhancing segmentation quality and improving precision for challenging structures like fluid regions. © 2026 IEEE.
