AB  - This paper uses deep semi-supervised learning methods to classify the Diabetes Foot Ulcer Challenge 2021 dataset and shows that using unlabeled data can effectively improve classification accuracy. Diabetes Foot Ulcer (DFU) is a global epidemic, which affects the security of life of about 100 million people. In recent years, the rapid development of deep learning has made it possible to reduce medical pressure. There are many deep learning methods for DFU medical image classification, but these works are isolated and lack systematic evaluation. In addition, there is little research on the problem of how to utilize unlabeled data effectively. We also find that using the Sharpness-Aware Minimization (SAM) optimization algorithm can further improve the precision and recall of the model. Finally, we got a macro f1-score of 0.5984, which is better than the official analysis results of DFUC2021.  © 2022 IEEE.
